### Rbac sample requests for the VS Code REST Client / Rider / Visual Studio.
###
### 1. Send the five login requests below.
### 2. Copy each accessToken from the response into the matching variable at the top of this file.
### 3. Send any of the demo requests. The comments state the expected status code.

@host = http://localhost:5010
@adminToken = paste-admin-accessToken
@managerToken = paste-manager-accessToken
@supportToken = paste-support-accessToken
@viewerToken = paste-viewer-accessToken
@auditorToken = paste-auditor-accessToken

### Login (anonymous) - Viewer gets orders:read from the role plus a direct reports:export grant.
# @name loginAdmin
POST {{host}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@rbac.dev",
  "password": "Admin!Pass123"
}

### Manager: rich, but no users:create / users:delete.
# @name loginManager
POST {{host}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "manager@rbac.dev",
  "password": "Manager!Pass123"
}

### Support: reads users and orders, cancels orders, creates nothing.
# @name loginSupport
POST {{host}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "support@rbac.dev",
  "password": "Support!Pass123"
}

### Viewer: read-only on orders, plus reports:export granted directly on the user.
# @name loginViewer
POST {{host}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "viewer@rbac.dev",
  "password": "Viewer!Pass123"
}

### Auditor: reports:read only.
# @name loginAuditor
POST {{host}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "auditor@rbac.dev",
  "password": "Auditor!Pass123"
}

### Who am I and what may I do?
GET {{host}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{viewerToken}}

### The whole RBAC configuration: every permission and the roles that carry it.
GET {{host}}/roles
Authorization: Bearer {{auditorToken}}

### 401 - no token at all.
GET {{host}}/users

### 403 - authenticated, but the token has no users:read.
GET {{host}}/users
Authorization: Bearer {{viewerToken}}

### 200 - Support holds users:read.
GET {{host}}/users
Authorization: Bearer {{supportToken}}

### 201 - Manager holds orders:create.
POST {{host}}/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{managerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerEmail": "customer@example.com",
  "description": "Ultrawide monitor",
  "total": 899.50
}

### 403 - the Viewer has no orders:create.
POST {{host}}/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{viewerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerEmail": "customer@example.com",
  "description": "Keyboard",
  "total": 149.00
}

### 200 - reports:read.
GET {{host}}/reports/summary
Authorization: Bearer {{auditorToken}}

### 200 - reports:export held by the Viewer as a direct grant (no role carries it for the Viewer).
GET {{host}}/reports/export
Authorization: Bearer {{viewerToken}}

### 403 - the Auditor can read reports but not export them.
GET {{host}}/reports/export
Authorization: Bearer {{auditorToken}}

### 200 - requires reports:read AND reports:export; the Manager holds both.
GET {{host}}/reports/full
Authorization: Bearer {{managerToken}}

### 403 - the Viewer holds only one of the two.
GET {{host}}/reports/full
Authorization: Bearer {{viewerToken}}

### Admin creates a user with two roles and one direct permission.
POST {{host}}/users
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "new.hire@rbac.dev",
  "password": "NewHire!Pass123",
  "firstName": "New",
  "lastName": "Hire",
  "roles": ["Viewer", "Auditor"],
  "permissions": ["orders:create"]
}

### Grant another permission directly (users:grant-permissions).
POST {{host}}/users/REPLACE-WITH-USER-ID/permissions
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "permissions": ["reports:export"],
  "revoke": false
}

### Replace a user's roles (users:assign-roles).
POST {{host}}/users/REPLACE-WITH-USER-ID/roles
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "roles": ["Manager"]
}

### Delete a user (users:delete).
DELETE {{host}}/users/REPLACE-WITH-USER-ID
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 400 - unknown role names are rejected with a validation problem.
POST {{host}}/users
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "wizard@rbac.dev",
  "password": "Wizard!Pass123",
  "firstName": "The",
  "lastName": "Wizard",
  "roles": ["Wizard"]
}
